{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChNLnxDCsPkmYzXbmKuh3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014PxZjHAMXTL9GZ6tbae3e7","name":"mcp__claudetto__patch","input":{"patch":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: PLAN.md\n+# Plan: skip blank-id rows in the importer\n+\n+Requirement (user's words): \"the importer must skip every row whose id is blank but keep rows whose id is the number zero, and log one line per skipped row with its line number\".\n+\n+## Repo state\n+\n+The repo holds only `README.md` (\"importer for rows\"). There is no importer code, language, input format or logger yet. This plan therefore fixes behaviour and tests. Implementation steps name no files until the importer exists.\n+\n+## Behaviour\n+\n+- **Skip** a row when its id is blank: missing, empty string, or only whitespace (and `null`/`None` if the input format can produce it).\n+- **Keep** a row when its id is the number zero. This covers `0`, `\"0\"`, and `0.0` if numbers are parsed. Do not test id with a truthiness check, because `0` is falsy in many languages. Use an explicit blank check (missing, null, or empty after trimming).\n+- **Log** exactly one line per skipped row, containing the line number. Kept rows produce no skip log.\n+- Line number: the 1-based line in the source file. If the file has a header row, the header is line 1 and the first data row is line 2. Count physical lines from the source, not the index among kept rows, so the number matches what the user sees in an editor.\n+\n+## Steps\n+\n+- Add `is_blank_id(value)`: true for missing, null, empty, or whitespace-only; false for `0` in every form.\n+- In the row loop, carry the source line number with each row, using the reader's own line counter and not a counter incremented only for kept rows.\n+- On a blank id, write one log line (for example `skipped line 7: blank id`) and continue. Do not raise.\n+- Keep all other validation unchanged.\n+\n+## Tests\n+\n+Tests call the importer's public interface and check the returned rows and the captured log output.\n+\n+- Blank id (empty, spaces, missing column value) gives no row and one log line with the correct line number.\n+- Id `0` gives a kept row and no log line.\n+- Mixed file: blank, `0`, normal, blank gives two kept rows and two log lines, with line numbers matching the source (header offset included).\n+- Two consecutive blank rows give two separate log lines.\n+- All rows blank gives an empty result, N log lines, and no error.\n+\n+## Open questions for the user\n+\n+- Is whitespace-only id \"blank\"? The plan assumes yes.\n+- Is `\"0\"` (string) treated the same as numeric `0`? The plan assumes yes.\n+- Which log destination and level? Unknown until a logger exists.\n+- Does the input have a header row, and are line numbers counted from it? The plan assumes 1-based physical lines, header included.\n*** End Patch"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":162,"cache_read_input_tokens":18665,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":162},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ebc17a44-865c-41dd-a73f-1b192e9f3e47","uuid":"2d27bc1f-ec02-444a-9a6e-07fab3a125dd","timestamp":"2026-11-24T19:56:30.998Z","request_id":"req_011ChNLnx4nJHytVTQ76omQd","tool_use_meta":[{"id":"toolu_014PxZjHAMXTL9GZ6tbae3e7","display_name":"Patch","server_display_name":"claudetto","tool_name":"patch"}]}
